+## Added in 0.7.1
+
+- `client` feature (on by default; see Features). A consumer that already used `default-features = false` and needs the client must now name `features = ["client"]`.
+- `LeasedPool::acquire_async` / `try_acquire_async`: the same single-flight, cooldown and epoch rules for an async `create`, on any executor; waiters park their task and never block a thread. Dropping the leader's future releases the key.
+- `LeasedPool::with_max_entries(n)`: a capacity cap. A full pool evicts the longest-idle unleased value, otherwise `try_acquire*` returns `AcquireError::PoolFull(snapshot)` (and `acquire*` returns `McpError::PoolFull`) without calling `create`.
+- `TrustStore::try_load_migrating` now sends a document whose `records` array does not parse as native records to the `migrate` hook.
+
